# Short URLs for links that travel off the site: a text message, a business
# card, something said out loud on a call. Nothing on the site links this way.
#
# The pages live at their .html paths and link to each other that way, which is
# what each one declares as its canonical. These rules only catch someone
# arriving at the short form from outside, and send them to the real address
# instead of leaving them on a 404.
#
# Netlify skips a redirect rule when the request already matches a file it can
# serve, so on a host that resolves extensionless paths by itself this rule is
# never reached. It is here so the short URL does not depend on that behaviour.
# tests/check-links.mjs flags extensionless links inside the site for the same
# reason: it is not guaranteed, so it should not be relied on silently.

/appointment    /appointment.html    301
